{{define "main"}}
<!-- Hero Section -->
<article class="triage-page">
    <section class="page-hero" id="rapid-exposure-triage-hero">
        <div class="hero-split">
            <div class="hero-split__copy">
                <div class="hero-kicker">
                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined icon-size-sm">policy</span>
                    <span class="eyebrow">A Focused, Authorized First Step</span>
                </div>
                <h1 class="hero-title">
                    Rapid Exposure Triage
                </h1>
                <p class="hero-description">
                    When vulnerability research moves faster, response needs to keep pace. AI is changing how quickly security research can progress. Tabiri uses AI-assisted workflows to turn relevant advisories into focused, authorized checks - with experienced security professionals reviewing the evidence and guiding next steps.
                </p>
                <div class="hero-actions hero-actions--left">
                    <a class="btn-primary" data-analytics-service-inquiry="rapid_exposure_triage" href="/contact?workflow_name=rapid-exposure-triage">Discuss an authorized triage</a>
                    <a class="btn-secondary" href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-split__visual">
                <div class="hero-split__glow"></div>
                <figure class="hero-split__frame">
                    <img alt="A vulnerability advisory moving through an authorized, shielded triage process to human review" class="hero-split__image hero-split__image--video" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="/static/images/rapid-exposure-triage-social.avif">
                </figure>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section content-section--muted content-section--border-bottom" id="triage-purpose">
        <div class="method-layout method-layout--compact">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Answer a focused question</p>
                <h2 class="section-heading">From <span class="section-heading__accent">new advisory</span> to a <span>clear next step</span></h2>
                <p class="body-copy body-copy--relaxed body-copy--first">
                    When a vulnerability is newly disclosed or a security concern needs quick investigation, teams may lack reliable version information or know which application paths matter. A bounded triage can gather relevant signals and help prioritize what engineers should verify next.
                </p>
                <p class="body-copy body-copy--relaxed">
                    Agent-assisted checks can accelerate evidence collection. Tabiri's security professionals review the evidence, explain its limitations, and help determine whether remediation, deeper validation, or another response is appropriate.
                </p>
            </div>
            <aside class="proof-card">
                <h3 class="proof-card__heading proof-card__heading--compact proof-card__heading--separated"><span>What triage is - and is not</span></h3>
                <ul class="triage-scope">
                    <li>A focused investigation of an agreed question and explicitly scoped systems.</li>
                    <li>A concise, human-reviewed account of checks, observations, uncertainty, and recommended next steps.</li>
                    <li>Not a full penetration test, a guarantee of safety, or automatic confirmation that a vulnerability is exploitable.</li>
                    <li>Not an unsolicited scan. An inquiry does not begin testing or grant permission to test.</li>
                </ul>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section content-section--light content-section--border-bottom" id="how-it-works">
        <div class="section-container">
            <div class="section-intro">
                <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">A controlled process</p>
                <h2 class="section-heading">Scope first. <span>Evidence second</span></h2>
                <p class="section-intro__description">We agree on the question and authorization before any technical testing begins.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-grid">
                <article class="trust-card-no-hover">
                    <div class="card-heading-row">
                        <div class="icon-tile"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">description</span></div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--primary">1. Confirm authority and scope</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="body-copy-small">Identify the asset owner and authorized requester, then document in-scope systems, permitted checks, timing, contacts, and stop conditions.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="trust-card-no-hover">
                    <div class="card-heading-row">
                        <div class="icon-tile"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">manage_search</span></div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--primary">2. Investigate the question</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="body-copy-small">Use agreed, appropriately bounded checks to collect relevant signals. Testing stays within the approved scope; potentially disruptive actions require separate agreement.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="trust-card-no-hover">
                    <div class="card-heading-row">
                        <div class="icon-tile"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">summarize</span></div>
                        <h3 class="heading-medium heading-medium--primary">3. Review and recommend</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="body-copy-small">An experienced reviewer summarizes observations and uncertainty, then discusses practical verification, remediation, or further assessment options.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section content-section--muted content-section--bordered" id="authorization">
        <div class="section-container">
            <div class="proof-card proof-card--narrow">
                <div class="method-note__content">
                    <div class="icon-tile proof-card__icon"><span class="material-symbols-outlined">verified_user</span></div>
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent eyebrow--compact">Permission is a prerequisite</p>
                        <h2 class="section-heading">No testing without <span>written authorization</span></h2>
                        <p class="body-copy body-copy--relaxed body-copy--separated">
                            Before testing, Tabiri must confirm written authorization from the asset owner or an authorized representative, along with the exact scope, allowed checks, timing, and escalation process. A matching business email and web domain can help verify a relationship, but it does not establish permission to test.
                        </p>
                        <p class="body-copy body-copy--relaxed">
                            Use the inquiry form to start a conversation only. Do not send credentials, secrets, or sensitive system data. We will not scan a domain just because it was submitted through the website.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section content-section--light content-section--border-bottom" id="triage-examples">
        <div class="section-container">
            <div class="section-intro">
                <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Examples of the approach</p>
                <h2 class="section-heading">Fast investigation. <span>Human judgment</span></h2>
                <p class="section-intro__description">See how Tabiri translated emerging vulnerability advisories into focused, authorized investigations without treating a signal as a verdict.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="triage-examples">
                <a class="trust-card group" href="/blog/how-tabiris-ai-agent-triaged-php2shell-safely-in-less-than-20-minutes">
                    <h3 class="triage-example__heading">PHP2Shell: a focused lead in about twenty minutes</h3>
                    <p class="body-copy-small">Read how an authorized environment was checked using targeted, non-exploit signals, with engineers responsible for confirming the system and risk.</p>
                </a>
                <a class="trust-card group" href="/blog/one-brotli-error-five-leads-how-tabirids-ai-agent-traced-node2shell-risk">
                    <h3 class="triage-example__heading">Node2Shell: five leads, not five confirmed vulnerabilities</h3>
                    <p class="body-copy-small">See how safe behavioral checks mapped potential exposure across authorized systems and directed human review.</p>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section content-section--muted content-section--bordered" id="related-services">
        <div class="section-container">
            <div class="section-intro">
                <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Choose the right next step</p>
                <h2 class="section-heading">Triage can connect to <span>broader security work</span></h2>
            </div>
            <div class="related-services">
                <a class="trust-card group" href="/penetration-testing">
                    <h3 class="related-services__heading">Deeper validation</h3>
                    <p class="body-copy-small-compact">Explore Tabiri's <strong>Penetration Testing</strong> service for validated findings and a practical remediation plan.</p>
                </a>
                <a class="trust-card group" href="/managed-cybersecurity-services">
                    <h3 class="related-services__heading">Ongoing visibility</h3>
                    <p class="body-copy-small-compact">Explore Tabiri's <strong>Managed Cybersecurity Services</strong> to track risk between assessments.</p>
                </a>
                <a class="trust-card group" href="/operational-assessment">
                    <h3 class="related-services__heading">Broader baseline</h3>
                    <p class="body-copy-small-compact">Explore Tabiri's <strong>Operational Assessment</strong> to connect technical observations to organizational priorities.</p>
                </a>
                <a class="trust-card group" href="/cybersecurity-insurance">
                    <h3 class="related-services__heading">Insurance readiness</h3>
                    <p class="body-copy-small-compact">Explore Tabiri's <strong>Cybersecurity Insurance</strong> service to discuss how security evidence can inform readiness, without guaranteeing coverage or pricing.</p>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="callout-section callout-section--unbordered callout-section--white" id="rapid-exposure-triage-cta">
        <div class="callout">
            <div class="callout__overlay"></div>
            <div class="callout__content callout__content--narrow">
                <p class="callout__eyebrow">Start with a conversation</p>
                <h2 class="callout__heading">Get clarity on your <span>next security decision</span></h2>
                <p class="callout__description">Tell us about the advisory or question. We will discuss whether triage is appropriate and confirm authority and scope before any testing.</p>
                <a class="btn-primary" data-analytics-service-inquiry="rapid_exposure_triage" href="/contact?workflow_name=rapid-exposure-triage">Discuss an authorized triage</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</article>
{{end}}
